[3] SELF-SIMILARITY of the gap: is G(S_d) governed by the single-digit gap?
    (G is dilation-invariant; the no-carry blocks are dilated copies at scale b^i)
    d=1: G(S_d)=0.40000   G(digits)=0.40000   ratio G_d/G_dig=1.0000
    d=2: G(S_d)=0.39900   G(digits)=0.40000   ratio G_d/G_dig=0.9975
    d=3: G(S_d)=0.39650   G(digits)=0.40000   ratio G_d/G_dig=0.9913
    => if G(S_d) stabilizes, the fractal has a scale-invariant gap (a 'fractal dimension')

[4] HASKELL lens: S_d = map (base-b eval) (replicateM d digits) — a d-fold fold;
    REP lens: p_{S_d} = Π_{i<d} D(x^{b^i}) (Riesz product / lacunary spectrum).
